    "swordCut": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IAutoMovieMotionHumanSword.ICut",
      "description": "Cut along one of the eight lines: the blade's landing part passes through the target at the decisive instant (`stroke`), edge leading. A target beyond the arm with the chosen advance is refused on `target`.\n\nThe contact pose puts the landing part (`LANDS.cut` along the held thing's edge, or its working point when it declares no edge) on the target with the edge along the travel, the blade's lean back and its turn about the travel chosen by the arm's fit (`HumanSwordLanding`); the stroke is that pose turned back by `SWING` about the axis square to blade and travel, the hilt going from a chamber by the shoulder to the contact on one progress, so the edge leads through the whole arc.\nThe aim, the contact pose, the chamber and the path, then the shared stroke planner.\n`SWING`, the leans and turns of the blade at contact and the chamber's place are provisional values named in code and documentation; an unreachable target is refused, never shortened.\nThe landing's fits (`HumanSwordLanding`), ending at the first the arm holds exactly; each posture costs the stroke planner's two elbow searches.\nPlanned once per instance; nothing is shared between instances.\nThe plan closes over its constants and the entry state, released with the plan."
    },
    "swordGuard": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IAutoMovieMotionHumanSwordGuard.IParams",
      "description": "Take a guard and hold it: the hilt reaches the guard's place after the setting time (`stroke`) and stays to the end.\n\nThe guard's row gives the hilt's place in arm lengths from the blade hand's shoulder and the blade's two directions in the performer's frame; the hand frame that holds the blade so is carried from the entry hold on the clock's minimum-jerk progress.\nOne table row, one pose, the shared stroke planner.\nThe setting time (0.5 s, scaled by recovery skill) and every row are provisional; a duration under the setting time is raised to it, as documented on `seconds`.\nConstant work per plan.\nPlanned once per instance; nothing is shared between instances.\nThe plan closes over its constants and the entry state, released with the plan."
    },
    "swordParry": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IAutoMovieMotionHumanSwordParry.IParry",
      "description": "Parry: the strong of the blade brought across an incoming blade where its attack is stopped, meeting it at `stroke`, or to a line as a drill. A meeting beyond the arm is refused on `target`; an attack without a blade on `against`.\n\nThe attacker's displayed blade at the attack's decisive instant gives the meeting point (`WEAK` of its length back from its point, the strong of the parrying blade on the weak of the attacking one); the parrying blade crosses it, upright for a high line and point down for a low one, offset to the defender's side by `HumanSword.GAP`. The parry waits in its entry hold so that its own travel ends on that instant.\nWhere the blades meet, the closed pose, the timing, then the shared stroke planner.\nThe meeting share, the hold and the retraction times are provisional; a parry that starts too late for its travel keeps its own time and arrives late, never faster than its skill.\nOne read of the attacker's prop frame per plan.\nPlanned once per instance; nothing is shared between instances.\nThe plan closes over its constants and the entry state, released with the plan."
    },
    "swordThrust": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IAutoMovieMotionHumanSword.IAttack",
      "description": "Thrust: the point driven straight onto the target at the decisive instant (`stroke`), with a step or a lunge when asked, then recovered. A target beyond the arm with the chosen advance, or so near that the hand would land within `NEAR` of the arm from the shoulder in a pose the arm cannot hold, is refused on `target`.\n\nThe landed pose puts the point on the target with the blade along the line from the shoulder, as it stands after the advance; the hilt starts drawn back beside the lower ribs with the point already on the line, and point and turn run to the landed pose on one progress. The attack lasts as a minimum-jerk unit arrested at its peak speed, the sword's cited peak velocity in a lunge.\nThe aim, the landed pose, the chamber, then the shared stroke planner.\nThe chamber's place is provisional; the shoulder used for the reach ignores the lunge's sink, stated at `StrikingBlade.shoulder`.\nConstant work per plan; each posture costs the stroke planner's elbow searches and, in an advance, one root lowering.\nPlanned once per instance; nothing is shared between instances.\nThe plan closes over its constants and the entry state, released with the plan."
    },
